{"id": 9328, "result": [{"value": {"choices": []}, "id": "jTukgOA6B5", "from_name": "flags", "to_name": "image", "type": "choices", "origin": "prediction"}, {"value": {"choices": ["Minor"]}, "id": "QfPHJXARet", "from_name": "severity", "to_name": "gpt-output", "type": "choices", "origin": "prediction-changed"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 3.5, "y": 12.7, "width": 30.8, "height": 10.6, "rotation": 0}, "id": "BB_1", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 3.5, "y": 12.7, "width": 30.8, "height": 10.6, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["text"]}, "id": "BB_1", "from_name": "label", "to_name": "image", "type": "labels", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 3.5, "y": 12.7, "width": 30.8, "height": 10.6, "rotation": 0, "text": ["6. \u00dcber einen\ndie Erregung und Ver\u00e4nderung des Lichtes\nbetreffenden heuristischen Gesichtspunkt;\nvon A. Einstein."]}, "id": "BB_1", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 2.299999999999999, "y": 25.50000000000002, "width": 33.299999999999976, "height": 41.54117647058821, "rotation": 0}, "id": "BB_2", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "prediction-changed"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 2.299999999999999, "y": 25.50000000000002, "width": 33.299999999999976, "height": 41.54117647058821, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["text"]}, "id": "BB_2", "from_name": "label", "to_name": "image", "type": "labels", "origin": "prediction-changed"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 2.299999999999999, "y": 25.50000000000002, "width": 33.299999999999976, "height": 41.54117647058821, "rotation": 0, "text": ["Zwischen den theoretischen Vorstellungen, welche sich die Physiker \u00fcber die Gase und andere ponderable K\u00f6rper gebildet haben, und der Maxwellschen Theorie der elektromagnetischen Prozesse im sogenannten leeren Raume besteht ein tiefgreifender formaler Unterschied. W\u00e4hrend wir uns n\u00e4mlich den Zustand eines K\u00f6rpers durch die Lage und Geschwindigkeiten einer zwar sehr gro\u00dfen, jedoch endlichen Anzahl von Atomen und Elektronen f\u00fcr vollkommen bestimmt annehmen, bedienen wir uns zur Bestimmung des elektromagnetischen Zustandes eines Raumes kontinuierlicher r\u00e4umlicher Funktionen, so da\u00df also eine endliche Anzahl von Gr\u00f6\u00dfen nicht als gegeben anzunehmen ist zur vollst\u00e4ndigen Festlegung des elektromagnetischen Zustandes eines Raumes. Nach der Maxwellschen Theorie ist bei allen rein elektromagnetischen Erscheinungen, also auch beim Licht, die Energie als kontinuierlich aufzufassen, w\u00e4hrend die Energie"]}, "id": "BB_2", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "prediction-changed"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 40.1, "y": 13.3, "width": 55.9, "height": 15.8, "rotation": 0}, "id": "BB_4", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 40.1, "y": 13.3, "width": 55.9, "height": 15.8, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["text"]}, "id": "BB_4", "from_name": "label", "to_name": "image", "type": "labels", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 40.1, "y": 13.3, "width": 55.9, "height": 15.8, "rotation": 0, "text": ["In what he considered the \"most radical\" of his papers of 1905, Einstein offered a \"heuristic\"\\* explanation of the photoelectric effect: What if light itself were quantized? "]}, "id": "BB_4", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 39.5, "y": 36.6, "width": 56.9, "height": 44.2, "rotation": 0}, "id": "BB_5", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 39.5, "y": 36.6, "width": 56.9, "height": 44.2, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["text"]}, "id": "BB_5", "from_name": "label", "to_name": "image", "type": "labels", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 39.5, "y": 36.6, "width": 56.9, "height": 44.2, "rotation": 0, "text": ["\"It seems to me that the observations about [...] the production of cathode rays by ultraviolet light [...] are more readily understood if one assumes that the energy of light is discontinuously distributed in space. [As suggested here,] the energy of a light ray spreading out from a point source is not continuously distributed over an increasing space but consists of a finite number of energy quanta which are localized at points in space, which move without dividing, and which can only be produced and absorbed as complete units.\""]}, "id": "BB_5", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 1, "y": 64.4, "width": 12.7, "height": 34.2, "rotation": 0}, "id": "BB_6", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_height": 360, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 1, "y": 64.4, "width": 12.7, "height": 34.2, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["image"]}, "id": "BB_6", "from_name": "label", "to_name": "image", "type": "labels", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 640, "original_hei